ready: 1
kind: operation
id: health.op.doctor
display_id: kernle.doctor
module: health
name: Kernle.doctor() · verify() · verify_memory(memory_type, memory_id) · find_orphaned_references()
summary: >-
  Checks the stack's integrity and setup, or one memory's provenance and versions, without
  changing anything.
notes: >-
  Each finding names the call that fixes it.
params:
  - { name: memory_type, type: str | None, source: "Caller, to check one memory", source_kind: parameter }
  - { name: memory_id, type: str | None, source: "Caller, to check one memory", source_kind: parameter }
returns: A list of checks, each passed, warning or failed, with details and the fixing call; exit status is non-zero on any failure from the command line.
sequence: health.seq.doctor
owner: crates/kernle-core/src/health/doctor.rs::doctor
tags:
  - { tag: cli, text: "kernle doctor, kernle verify, kernle audit" }
